# Square Recovery Package Subscription Setup

The recovery-support package buttons are wired to Square hosted checkout for monthly recurring billing.

## What the site expects

Create four monthly Square subscription plan variations, then add their variation IDs to Vercel environment variables:

| ComCare package | Monthly price | Vercel environment variable |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Essential Recovery | $49/month | `SQUARE_RECOVERY_ESSENTIAL_PLAN_VARIATION_ID` |
| Comfort Recovery | $149/month | `SQUARE_RECOVERY_COMFORT_PLAN_VARIATION_ID` |
| Comfort Extend | $249/month | `SQUARE_RECOVERY_EXTEND_PLAN_VARIATION_ID` |
| Comfort Plus | $399/month | `SQUARE_RECOVERY_PLUS_PLAN_VARIATION_ID` |

Keep these existing Square variables too:

```env
SQUARE_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_square_access_token_here
SQUARE_APPLICATION_ID=your_square_application_id_here
SQUARE_LOCATION_ID=your_square_location_id_here
```

## How the checkout works

1. Customer clicks a package button on `recovery-support.html`.
2. `script.js` posts the selected package code to `/create-checkout-session`.
3. `api/create-checkout-session.js` creates a Square hosted checkout link using:
   - the package monthly price
   - the package Square subscription plan variation ID
   - `subscription_plan_id`
4. Square collects the card, creates the subscription, emails the receipt, and continues monthly billing.
5. Square redirects the customer back to `home.html?checkout=subscription-success`.

## Important Square requirement

Square's Checkout API needs the ID of the subscription plan variation, not just the parent subscription plan. In Square API field naming this is still passed as `subscription_plan_id`.

Official Square docs:

- https://developer.squareup.com/docs/checkout-api/subscription-plan-checkout
- https://developer.squareup.com/docs/subscriptions-api/manage-subscriptions
